WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.187
This is the journal browser. It answers

2
00:00:03.187 --> 00:00:05.972
the question every researcher faces: where

3
00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:08.758
should I publish? Which journals sit under

4
00:00:08.758 --> 00:00:11.080
our open access deals? What will it

5
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.467
cost? And how much does my institute

6
00:00:13.467 --> 00:00:14.595
already use them?

7
00:00:15.295 --> 00:00:18.228
Journal Browser is a public search tool

8
00:00:18.228 --> 00:00:21.162
built on openly available data only. It

9
00:00:21.162 --> 00:00:24.170
replaces the old WUR hosted browser, and

10
00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:26.802
any Dutch institute can run its own

11
00:00:26.802 --> 00:00:29.811
instance. Set the institution variables,

12
00:00:29.811 --> 00:00:32.744
run docker compose up, and the database

13
00:00:32.744 --> 00:00:35.076
fills itself. One codebase, any

14
00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:35.903
university.

15
00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:39.637
The stack is deliberately boring, on

16
00:00:39.637 --> 00:00:43.007
purpose. A FastAPI backend on SQLAlchemy

17
00:00:43.007 --> 00:00:46.546
two. Postgres seventeen with pgvector. And

18
00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.748
a Next.js fifteen frontend. Everything

19
00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:53.035
ships as four containers in one compose

20
00:00:53.035 --> 00:00:53.456
file.

21
00:00:54.156 --> 00:00:56.624
The signature piece is the bootstrap

22
00:00:56.624 --> 00:00:59.024
pipeline. On first boot, a one shot

23
00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:01.903
container runs a dependency graph of about

24
00:01:01.903 --> 00:01:04.714
thirty jobs. First, a global layer sweeps

25
00:01:04.714 --> 00:01:07.457
the journal universe and builds the deal

26
00:01:07.457 --> 00:01:10.062
register. Then a per institution layer

27
00:01:10.062 --> 00:01:12.873
harvests each university's works. The API

28
00:01:12.873 --> 00:01:15.409
stays down until every step succeeds.

29
00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:17.946
Every job is idempotent, so a failure

30
00:01:17.946 --> 00:01:20.140
names its step and reruns clean.

31
00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:24.006
Ten external sources feed that pipeline.

32
00:01:24.006 --> 00:01:27.093
Pure provides the canonical publication

33
00:01:27.093 --> 00:01:30.022
corpus. OpenAlex supplies the journal

34
00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:32.793
universe. openaccess.nl is the deal

35
00:01:32.793 --> 00:01:35.959
register. And DOAJ, OpenAPC, and Scimago

36
00:01:35.959 --> 00:01:39.205
add OA status, costs, and quartiles. Each

37
00:01:39.205 --> 00:01:41.896
source has its own harvest module.

38
00:01:42.596 --> 00:01:45.433
Everything keys on ISSN-L. One sweep turns

39
00:01:45.433 --> 00:01:47.729
about two hundred seventy thousand

40
00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:50.498
OpenAlex sources into one hundred seventy

41
00:01:50.498 --> 00:01:52.727
seven thousand journals. Evidence

42
00:01:52.727 --> 00:01:55.428
denormalizes onto each row. DOAJ status,

43
00:01:55.428 --> 00:01:57.725
latest APC cost, Scimago quartile,

44
00:01:57.725 --> 00:02:00.291
publisher lineage, and a three hundred

45
00:02:00.291 --> 00:02:02.655
eighty four dimension embedding for

46
00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:05.356
semantic search. For Twente, the serving

47
00:02:05.356 --> 00:02:07.855
scope is about one hundred forty four

48
00:02:07.855 --> 00:02:09.071
thousand journals.

49
00:02:09.771 --> 00:02:12.280
Works live in one table, keyed by

50
00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:15.168
institution and Pure ID. Each DOI gets

51
00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:18.285
confirmed against OpenAIRE, OpenAlex, and

52
00:02:18.285 --> 00:02:20.945
Crossref. Authors resolve through a

53
00:02:20.945 --> 00:02:23.910
cascade. ORCID exact match first, fuzzy

54
00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.951
match last, always gated by affiliation.

55
00:02:26.951 --> 00:02:29.915
Candidate matches wait for admin review

56
00:02:29.915 --> 00:02:32.576
instead of becoming facts silently.

57
00:02:33.276 --> 00:02:36.343
Serving is where it comes together. Full

58
00:02:36.343 --> 00:02:39.410
text search with faceted filters, cached

59
00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:42.477
behind an epoch counter. Semantic search

60
00:02:42.477 --> 00:02:45.620
rides pgvector with an HNSW index. Search

61
00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.611
scopes cover all, title, publisher, and

62
00:02:48.611 --> 00:02:51.754
topic fields. Open access type is derived

63
00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:54.591
at query time. Gold, diamond, hybrid,

64
00:02:54.591 --> 00:02:56.508
generic, or subscription.

65
00:02:57.208 --> 00:03:00.543
The API exposes forty two operations under

66
00:03:00.543 --> 00:03:03.401
/api/v1. Admin and feedback mount as

67
00:03:03.401 --> 00:03:06.577
global routes. Everything else scopes to

68
00:03:06.577 --> 00:03:09.673
an institution code in the path. Cursor

69
00:03:09.673 --> 00:03:12.849
pagination keeps every list stable while

70
00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:16.025
harvests run. CI regenerates the OpenAPI

71
00:03:16.025 --> 00:03:18.803
schema on every push, and fails the

72
00:03:18.803 --> 00:03:20.312
build if it drifts.

73
00:03:21.012 --> 00:03:24.166
The frontend is Next.js fifteen with React

74
00:03:24.166 --> 00:03:26.569
Query. Every page lives under an

75
00:03:26.569 --> 00:03:29.122
institution segment, so Twente and

76
00:03:29.122 --> 00:03:32.275
Groningen share one codebase. Filter state

77
00:03:32.275 --> 00:03:34.453
lives in the URL, so any view

78
00:03:34.453 --> 00:03:36.180
you build is shareable.

79
00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.780
That is the multi institution core. One

80
00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.679
deployment hosts many universities over

81
00:03:42.679 --> 00:03:45.654
one shared data core. Journals and deals

82
00:03:45.654 --> 00:03:48.330
store once. Institution labels, data

83
00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:51.304
windows, and library links are rows, not

84
00:03:51.304 --> 00:03:54.353
code. Onboarding a second institute takes

85
00:03:54.353 --> 00:03:56.955
one SQL update and one harvest run.

86
00:03:57.655 --> 00:04:00.002
The pace tells its own story. Two

87
00:04:00.002 --> 00:04:02.917
hundred forty eight commits in nine days,

88
00:04:02.917 --> 00:04:05.264
all by one developer. Forty three

89
00:04:05.264 --> 00:04:07.824
migrations. Forty seven backend test

90
00:04:07.824 --> 00:04:10.668
files. Three hundred twenty nine tracked

91
00:04:10.668 --> 00:04:11.095
files.

92
00:04:11.795 --> 00:04:14.883
So, one command bootstraps a fully sourced

93
00:04:14.883 --> 00:04:17.677
publication browser for any institute.

94
00:04:17.677 --> 00:04:20.765
Search journals by deal coverage, cost, or

95
00:04:20.765 --> 00:04:23.485
meaning. The repo is journal browser.

96
00:04:23.485 --> 00:04:26.132
DEPLOYMENT.md carries the operations

97
00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.926
detail, and the wiki carries the rest.
